From 6def40f98c64ed83be50a84b70d4d9e2a2068ff2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Pray <nickwpray@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:55:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fork: voice follows Default send and ducks instead of
 interrupting

Speaking in voice mode while the agent works now follows the Default send
setting: steer folds the transcript into the running turn, queue adds it
to the composer queue (merging consecutive spoken items), and interrupt
keeps the old behaviour. Agent speech fades to a whisper while the user
talks and fades back after, so echo can no longer cancel a run. Queue
rows get Edit, Remove and Interrupt and send now. The thinking tone fades
in and out on its own gain stage. Gated on features.voiceSendBehavior;
native ducking is a guarded no-op until the native gain lands.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
